tags: [[Profile Picker]]
title: Flatten Toggle
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Most sources need nothing here, and the checkbox can be ignored.

It matters when your source reports every field as its own object — `{"key": "date", "value": "9/16/26", "type": "string", "array": false}` — instead of as the plain pair `"date": "9/16/26"`.  Text-extraction and form-parsing tools do this fairly often.  Left alone, such a source gives you a record whose only visible leaves are `key`, `value`, `type` and `array`, repeated once per field, and there is no sensible way to write a binding against it.

Tick ''Flatten key/value pair arrays'' and JSON Convert collapses those arrays into ordinary objects before the records path is resolved.  `{{fields.date}}` then works, and the ''Browse…'' trees list the real field names.

The setting belongs to the ''profile'', not to the session: ticking it rewrites the selected profile to include a `normalize` step, so the next import of the same shape is already configured.  The profile editor carries the same checkbox above the records path.  Untick it and the step is removed again.

For what the step actually does, its options, and the warnings it can raise, see [[Normalize]] in the Profile Guide.  [[Example Reified Output]] is a worked profile you can run against [[Example Reified Output Data]].
